      "title": "One extra measurement halves qubit errors",
      "summary": "Researchers at the University of Regensburg and partners showed that adding a single measurement before a series of quantum operations can cut the error rate by more than half. This is a step forward because errors are the main obstacle to useful quantum computers, and this fix is cheap. It was shown in an experiment, so it still has to be tested on larger machines with many qubits.",
